==Maori==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|mi|poz-pol-pro|*taqe}} (compare with {{cog|sm|tae}} and {{cog|to|taʻe}}),<ref>{{cite-book|title=Maori-Polynesian Comparative Dictionary|first= Edward|last=Tregear|year=1891|publisher=Lyon and Blair |location=Wellington, New Zealand|pages=439-40|url=https://nzetc.victoria.ac.nz/tm/scholarly/tei-TreMaor-c1-12.html}}</ref> from {{inh|mi|poz-oce-pro|*taqe}} (compare with {{cog|fj|de}}), from {{inh|mi|poz-pro|*taqi}} (compare with {{cog|ms|tahi}}, {{cog|tl|tae}}).<ref name=P>{{R:Pollex|taqe.1}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book |pages=202-3| first = Malcolm D.  | last = Ross | first2=Andrew |last2= Pawley |first3=Meredith |last3=Osmond | year=  2016 | title = The lexicon of Proto-Oceanic | volume = 5: People, body and mind | location = Canberra | publisher = Australian National University | isbn = 9781922185327 }}</ref>

====Noun====
{{mi-noun}}

# [[excrement]], [[filth]]
#: {{syn|mi|tūtae|weta|roke}}
# [[sap]] or [[gum]] excreted from plants
# [[refuse]], [[waste]], [[rubbish]]
#: {{syn|mi|para|maumau}}

===Etymology 2===
Likely related to etymology 1 with semantic evolution from "[plant] excretion" or "residue" > "stain" hence broadening to dyes; compare also with {{cog|ms|tahi}} for similar patterns. {{rfe|mi}}

====Noun====
{{mi-noun}}
# [[stain]]
# [[dye]], [[pigment]]
# [[colour]]
#: {{syn|mi|mura|kano}}

=====References=====
<references/>

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|mi|poz-pol-pro|*tae}} (“to reach, to arrive” – compare with {{cog|ty|tae}} “to arrive or reach somewhere”, {{cog|sm|taea}} “to reach to somewhere”, {{cog|to|tae}} “to reach for an object by stretching one's hand” and {{m|to|tatae}} “to extend the arm to collect; to gather”).<ref>{{cite-book|title=Maori-Polynesian Comparative Dictionary|first= Edward|last=Tregear|year=1891|publisher=Lyon and Blair |location=Wellington, New Zealand|pages=439-40|url=https://nzetc.victoria.ac.nz/tm/scholarly/tei-TreMaor-c1-12.html}}</ref><ref name=P>{{R:Pollex|taqe.1}}</ref> {{rfe|mi}}

====Verb====
{{mi-verb}}
# to [[arrive]] at or to somewhere
#: {{syn|mi|haere}}
# to [[extend]] towards, to [[reach]]
# to [[proceed]]

